A||||10||Ralph||International Research Motorsports (IRM)||||1||
Z||000000||Ralph||08-31-2000||05:50 PM||||Only to anyone interested.....<BR>I have seen some chatter about IRM. They are still in business. Since they are very close to my location I decided to find out. Yep, they sure are. As a matter of fact it only took two days to get a catalog from them and it is loaded. They even included a couple of photos because I was inquiring about quarter panel scoops. <BR>They are located in Rockville, Maryland (in the DC suburbs) Ph 301-948-3301 or 800-367-8423. I am neither endorsing or recommending this company. Merely providing information.<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/yellowformula/LittleFiero.jpg">  <BR>  <B>  Ralph </B><p>[This message has been edited by Ralph (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||08-31-2000||07:41 PM||||I checked out there web-site and found out that they sell a turbo kit for the fiero. It costs about $2900 for the manual and $2600 for the automatic transmissions. I thought that Design One was the only one that sold a turbo kit. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-31-2000||09:28 PM||||I have heard that the IRM turbo <I>is</I> the Design One kit. <BR>All hearsay, mind you.  <P>I am glad to hear that they are still in business. Bought a few things from them in the past. They seem like good folks. <BR>Thought that Jim's health problems might be a show stopper. Thankfully, that wasn't the case.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
