Z||000008||Monkeyman||09-01-2000||01:05 PM||||I just got off of the phone with Barbara @ IRM.  She said that her husband is doing better and that they will go out of business when (and if) she ever dies.  She said that she's a little behind in her work (to be expected) but she's still there.  Their email addy is: irmfiero@aol.com in case any one is interested.<P>I inquired about a real website for them.  She said that she doesn't know enough about it to make it happen and doesn't have the time.  I asked if she would consider a site if someone else did it for her (and kept it maintained) for cheap.  She said that she and her husband would consider it.  I know that there are some mighty smart (computer literate) members out there in her neck of the woods.  If anyone is interested in supporting a site for IRM, please email her directly.  Most of the other major part players have a site.  IRM should too, IMHO.  Surely someone can help her out???||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||09-05-2000||12:33 PM||||Monkeyman: I don't have email access at the moment (I'm working on that though.. hopefully by the end of the week) but I think I'd be able to help them out! In fact, I'd love to... I'd really appreciate it if you could let them know I'm interested in helping them get online (for a very reasonable price).. thanks a million..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
